<!--
    App settings, edited in Garmin Connect Mobile / Garmin Express.

    THESE DO NOT REACH A SIDELOADED APP. Measured on a fenix 8, 2026-08-27:
    with this file built in and the strings verified present in the shipped
    .prg ("proxyServerProp" at offset 8725 of a 168 KB debug build), neither
    Garmin Connect nor the Connect IQ app showed any settings page for the
    app at all. Garmin renders the settings UI from the app's STORE LISTING,
    not by reading the definition off the device, and a sideloaded app has no
    listing - so there is nothing for the phone to draw.

    Kept anyway, because it costs one guarded no-op property read per entry
    point and starts working the day this app is published. Until then the
    watch's own TextPicker rows are the only way in, and the 31-character cap
    they carry is what makes a short hostname necessary. Do not spend another
    cycle trying to make this appear on a sideloaded install.

    Only the two long values live here. Speed and quality stay on the watch,
    where they can be cycled in one tap with no phone in range - the split is
    "what you paste once comes from the phone, what you change often stays on
    the wrist", which also means neither setting has two places to edit it.

    The server is type="url" rather than alphaNumeric because that is the type
    designed to carry one, and alphaNumeric's name is ambiguous enough about
    ':' and '/' not to be worth the risk. It wants the full address including
    the scheme; there is no length pressure here, unlike the watch's picker.
-->
<settings>
    <setting propertyKey="@Properties.proxyServerProp"
             title="@Strings.settingServer"
             prompt="@Strings.settingServerPrompt">
        <settingConfig type="url" />
    </setting>

    <setting propertyKey="@Properties.proxyTokenProp"
             title="@Strings.settingToken"
             prompt="@Strings.settingTokenPrompt">
        <settingConfig type="password" />
    </setting>
</settings>
